title: Tackle Turn Cancellation Tasks
status: draft
created: 2026-10-24
author: adrian
items[11]{id,title,description,criteria,complexity,effort,dependencies,refs}:
  T-001,[x] Cancellation registry,"Add `tokio-util` as a direct dependency in `crates/agentkit-tackle/Cargo.toml` with its `rt` feature. Add `cancellations: Mutex<BTreeMap<String, CancellationToken>>` to `ConnectionNegotiation` in `acp_v1/negotiation.rs`, plus `register(session) -> (CancellationToken, CancelRegistration)` and a `cancel(session)` lookup. `CancelRegistration` is a drop guard that removes the session's entry, so cleanup happens on every exit path.","Unit tests: registering a session yields a token; `cancel` triggers it; dropping the guard removes the entry; cancelling twice and cancelling after the guard drops are no-ops; `cargo test -p agentkit-tackle` passes",low,"2-3h",,"single-primitive,no-new-dependency-tree,cleanup-on-cancel"
  T-002,[x] Thread the token into the turn,"Add a `cancellation: CancellationToken` field to `TurnRuntime` in `agent/runtime.rs` and set it from the registered token in `acp_v1/support.rs::turn_runtime`. Thread it through `run_prompt_turn` to `run_turn_loop` and into `run_turn`. No behavioural change yet: the token is carried but not observed.","The crate compiles and the existing suite passes unchanged; a trivial observation test confirms the token reaches `run_turn`",low,"1-2h",T-001,"single-primitive,one-mechanism"
  T-003,[x] Observe cancellation in the turn loop,"In `agent/turn.rs::run_turn`, accumulate streamed text in a shared buffer (the `on_delta` closure appends to it as well as forwarding) and wrap the `provider.stream_completion` await in a biased `tokio::select!` against `token.cancelled()`. On cancel persist the buffered partial text under `message_id`, then return `TurnOutcome { stop: TurnStop::Cancelled }`. Check `token.is_cancelled()` at the top of each loop iteration and select the tool-call await, so a cancelled turn issues no further request. Add `TurnStop::Cancelled` in `agent/outcome.rs`.","A stub provider that never completes, with a cancelled token, makes `run_turn` return `Cancelled` promptly and persist the partial text; a token cancelled between requests stops the loop without issuing a new request; an already-completed token does not disturb a normal turn; existing turn tests pass",high,"3-4h",T-002,"partial-output-persisted,one-mechanism,no-updates-after-response,idempotent-cancellation"
  T-004,[x] Register the token around the spawned turn,"In `acp_v1/prompt.rs`, create and register a token for the spawned model turn before `cx.spawn`, and hold the `CancelRegistration` guard inside the spawned task so the entry is removed when the turn ends. Direct `/!` invocations and the fast command intercepts (fork, `/mcp`, `/editor`, `/context`, compaction) are not registered: they do not observe the token, so a registration would be inert.","The registry unit tests cover register/cancel/drop; a model turn runs against the registered token and deregisters on completion; existing prompt tests pass",medium,"2-3h","T-001,T-002,T-003","session-cancel,cleanup-on-cancel,one-mechanism"
  T-005,[x] Cancelled stop reason and finalisation,"Map `TurnStop::Cancelled` to `StopReason::Cancelled` in the `run_model_turn_case` response match in `acp_v1/prompt.rs`. Confirm the cancelled path still reports session info, fires the detached hooks, releases the lease, and removes the registry entry.","A cancelled turn's `session/prompt` response carries `stopReason: cancelled`; the session's lease is free immediately after; exactly one response is sent and no content or tool-call update follows it",low,"1-2h","T-003,T-004","session-cancel,cleanup-on-cancel,no-updates-after-response"
  T-006,[x] session/cancel handler,"Register an `on_receive_notification` handler for `CancelNotification` (`session/cancel`) in the `acp_v1/server.rs` builder. The handler resolves the store session id, looks up the token in the connection registry, and cancels it; unknown sessions are ignored.","An integration test sends `session/cancel` for a session with an in-flight prompt and the prompt resolves cancelled; a cancel for an idle or unknown session is a no-op that sends nothing",low,"1-2h",T-004,"session-cancel,cancel-after-completion,unknown-session"
  T-007,session/close cancels the turn,"In `acp_v1/sessions.rs::handle_close_session`, cancel the session's token before the existing close work (store close, grant clear, terminal release). The close request still returns its normal response.","An integration test sends `session/close` while a prompt is in flight: the prompt resolves cancelled, the close response still arrives, and the session remains listable with grants cleared and terminals released; close on an idle session is unchanged",low,"1-2h",T-004,"close-cancels,idle-close"
  T-008,$/cancel_request bridge,"In `acp_v1/prompt.rs::run_model_turn_case`, capture `responder.cancellation()` before the responder moves into the spawned task, and cancel the same token when that marker fires, bridging the SDK's per-request cancellation.","An integration test sends `$/cancel_request` for an in-flight prompt and receives exactly one response: a valid PromptResponse with `stopReason: cancelled`; a request that completes before the cancel still gets its normal response",medium,"2-3h",T-004,"cancel-request,idempotent-cancellation,race-with-completion"
  T-009,Cancellation integration tests,"Extend the existing in-process ACP integration harness with cancellation coverage: cancel during a streamed turn, cancel during a tool call including an open permission request, close during a turn, and the cancellation race. Assert no content or tool-call update arrives after the cancelled response, the lease is released, and cancelling a turn stops a nested agent loop it spawned.","The new tests run offline; `cargo test -p agentkit-tackle` passes; they fail if a late update follows the response, if the lease is not released, or if a cancelled tool call still completes",medium,"3-4h","T-005,T-006,T-007,T-008","transcript-coverage,no-updates-after-response,cancel-during-tool-call,connection-drops,nested-agent-loop"
  T-010,Golden-transcript cancel coverage,"Add transcript steps covering a cancelled turn and a close during a turn to `crates/agentkit-tackle/tests/acp_v1_conformance.rs` and `tests/transcripts`, keeping the existing subset-match semantics.","The transcript suite replays a cancelled prompt asserting `stopReason: cancelled` and fails if a late notification follows the response; `cargo test -p agentkit-tackle acp_v1_conformance` passes",low,"2-3h","T-005,T-006","transcript-coverage,graceful-idle-close"
  T-011,Conformance run and baseline reseed,"Ensure the deterministic test model exercises `$/cancel_request` if the current sentinel flow does not, run `just tackle conformance`, and confirm `ACP-CANCEL-001`, `ACP-CANCEL-002`, `ACP-CLOSE-002` and `ACP-JSONRPC-007` pass rather than skip. Reseed `crates/agentkit-tackle/tests/conformance/baseline.txt` with `just tackle seed-baseline` and review the diff.","The four requirements report PASS in `target/conformance/report.json`; the seeded baseline no longer lists them; `just tackle check-baseline` reports no new failures and no drift",medium,"2-3h","T-009,T-010","cancel-conformance,close-conformance,cancel-request-conformance,baseline-tightened"
